{"metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"chord","symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"chord","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Chord","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLHarmonyV5ChordV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLHarmonyV5chordSayAC5ChordVGvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"chord","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmony\/Chord-swift.struct","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLHarmonyV5ChordV","text":"Chord","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A root is a pitch name like C, D, E, while a numeral is a scale degree like 1, 2, 3. The root element is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"generally used with pop chord symbols, while the numeral element is generally used with classical functional"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"harmony and Nashville numbers. It is an either\/or choice to avoid data inconsistency. The function element,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which represents Roman numerals with roman numeral text, has been deprecated as of MusicXML 4.0."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<harmony-chord>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarmony\/chord-swift.property"},